('MR-15','Cross-cutting governance, privacy and annual reuse','Protect assessment information, limit personal data (no beneficiary or CBMS personal data copied into the assessment), maintain City-controlled storage, audit changes and support annual self-assessment.','IAT QA/Ethics/Data Privacy; RA 10173; annual self-assessment objective','All 140','Access controls, audit logs, privacy controls, versioned records','Method limitations/privacy statement','MOO governance/update mechanism','RBAC/RLS; audit trail; versioning; annual cycle cloning','users; roles; audit_logs; document_versions; assessment_cycles','Privacy breach risk is always High','Critical',15),
('MR-16','Statutory: RA 12287 and IRR (anticipatory action)','Be ready to request, declare, implement, fund, lift and report a State of Imminent Disaster, and to take anticipatory action within the lead time, including city-level early action for short-lead-time hazards (flash floods, landslides).','RA 12287; IRR signed 14 Sep 2026 (Rules II–VII); IAT v1.1 Annex G §5','A1.8; A2.8; A2.9; A4.6; A5.8; A6.2; A6.7; A7.6; A8.6; A8.8; A8.9; A10.8; B1.2; B6.6; C2.1; C2.2; C2.3; C3.3; C4.1; C4.2; C4.3; C4.4','SOP and EO templates; RDRRMC request records; AA protocols; LDRRMFIP AA line; advisory templates; targeting guidelines; 45-day reports','§5 Readiness under RA 12287','MOO Ch.1 declaration procedure; MOO Ch.4 AA protocols; MOO Ch.5 AA funding; MOO Ch.7 reporting; EOC Ch.2 anticipatory posture','Declaration workflow (PDRA → CDRRMC → RDRRMC 24-hour reply → Mayor''s EO → lifting); AA checklist by hazard and lead time; AA fund tracker with 30%/70% tranche rule; 45-day report generator','declarations; pdras; aa_protocols; aa_triggers; prepositioning_orders; aa_fund_allocations; beneficiary_targeting; declaration_reports','Escalate weight-3 Mandatory AA gaps to the Mayor and CDRRMC before typhoon season','Critical',16),
('MR-17','Interface indicators (Part C)','Assess, separately from the CDRRMO''s own index, city systems owned by other offices that the CDRRMO depends on, and route each gap to the named lead office.','IAT v1.1 Part C; UNDRR Scorecard; RA 12287 IRR Rule IV Secs. 4, 8–10','C1.1–C5.1 (15 indicators)','Lead-office records; short KIIs with lead offices','§6 Results for Part C, by lead office','MOO Ch.3 and Ch.9 coordination arrangements; EOC Ch.4 and Ch.7 sector desks','Lead-office assignment; separate Interface Index; inter-office action tracking','interface_offices; interface_responses; inter_office_actions','High only at weight 3 and score ≤1 (Good Practice factor)','High',17),
('MR-18','Framework alignment: UNDRR Disaster Resilience Scorecard','Keep each Scorecard-derived indicator traceable to its DRSC criterion so results can feed MCR2030 and Sendai reporting; Scorecard criteria not adopted stay for a city-wide Scorecard workshop and are not scored.','UNDRR DRSC Detailed Level Assessment (2017); IAT v1.1 Crosswalk','A2.10; A4.9; A5.7; A5.8; A5.9; A7.6; A7.8; A7.9; A9.5; A10.2; A10.9; B5.7; B6.6; C1.1; C1.2; C1.3; C1.4; C2.1; C2.2; C2.3; C3.1; C3.2; C5.1','DRSC reference in each indicator; Framework_Crosswalk sheet','§2 Background and method; Crosswalk annex','MOO Ch.7 M&E and reporting','Framework crosswalk view; external framework tags on indicators','framework_refs; indicator_framework_links','Deferred criteria are not scored','Medium',18)
